#8800
A Coastal Peninsula~
   You stand at the edge of the great forest, on a small, wooded peninsula
that juts out into the ocean to form a narrow, natural breakwater. A few
shattered and weather-worn boulders lie scattered about the pines, anchoring
the trees in place. The only exit is to the south, back along the wooded coast.
~
88 m 3
D1
~
~
0 0 21400
D2
~
~
0 0 8801
S
#8801
The Coast~
   You stand at the edge of the great forest, on the coast of an ocean that
spreads as far as the eye can see. To the west, thick underbrush blocks your
path.
~
