#8802
A Spring near the Coast~
   You stand at the edge of the great forest, on the coast of an ocean that
spreads as far as the eye can see. Here, a natural spring bubbles up from
a jumble of rocks at the forest's edge, trickling toward the ocean in a thin
rivulet. The coastline continues to the north and south.
~
